    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0422" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.1153 Smith Company, Werner G./35:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-25T16:00:00+08:00">July 25, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 25—12:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s July 23, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="33" xml:id="d559-f1"/> Werner G. Smith
                    Company state that, owing to probability losses through leakage in case oil
                    transferred to godown, company desires that American authorities continue
                    efforts to obtain unconditional release of wood oil.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai, Nanking. Shanghai please repeat to Tokyo. Copy to the
                    Embassy, Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
